          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Marie Antoinette</strong><br>\nBorn on November 2, 1755, in Vienna, Austria, Marie Antoinette was the youngest daughter of Emperor Francis I and Empress Maria Theresa. She grew up in the luxurious atmosphere of the Austrian court and was married at the age of 14 to the future King Louis XVI of France. Her education included music, dance, and the social graces but lacked a formal understanding of political affairs, which later affected her role as queen.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Marriage to Louis XVI</strong><br>\nMarie Antoinette married Louis-Auguste, who became King Louis XVI of France, in 1770. Her marriage was an alliance between Austria and France, meant to solidify the relationship between the two powers. Initially, her marriage was challenging due to Louis XVI's reserved personality and the couple's lack of experience. However, they eventually formed a closer relationship and had four children together.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Life at Versailles</strong><br>\nAs Queen of France, Marie Antoinette's life at the Palace of Versailles was under constant scrutiny. She was known for her extravagant fashion, elaborate hairstyles, and love of parties, which sometimes drew criticism from the French populace. Despite her personal charm, she struggled to navigate the complex and often vicious politics of the French court.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
