            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Public Perception</strong><br>\nThe French public had a mixed view of Marie Antoinette. She was often criticized for her Austrian heritage and extravagant spending, which earned her the nickname \"Madame Deficit\" during a time of financial crisis in France. Rumors and slander in pamphlets further tarnished her reputation, exacerbating the public's resentment towards the monarchy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Queen's Image</strong><br>\nEfforts were made to improve Marie Antoinette's image. She was portrayed in artworks and propaganda as a caring mother and modest queen. However, these attempts were overshadowed by France's dire economic conditions and the queen's earlier image as a spendthrift, which continued to dominate public opinion.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Role in Politics</strong><br>\nMarie Antoinette's role in politics grew over time, especially after the outbreak of the French Revolution in 1789. She was initially disinterested in state affairs, but her influence increased as Louis XVI's reign faced turmoil. She corresponded with other European leaders and took a more active role in advising the king, with mixed results.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
