          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The French Revolution</strong><br>\nThe French Revolution dramatically changed Marie Antoinette's life. The monarchy was abolished, and she was stripped of her title and privileges. Her family was imprisoned, and she faced hostility and contempt from the revolutionaries. Her life became a symbol of the excesses of the monarchy that the Revolution sought to obliterate.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Imprisonment and Trial</strong><br>\nMarie Antoinette was imprisoned with her family in the Temple prison before being transferred to the Conciergerie, a bleak and foreboding jail. She was separated from her children and subjected to a trial by the Revolutionary Tribunal. Accused of high treason and other charges, her fate became a foregone conclusion amidst the Revolution's radical phase.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Execution of Marie Antoinette</strong><br>\nMarie Antoinette was executed by guillotine on October 16, 1793, at the Place de la Révolution in Paris. Her death marked a turning point in the Revolution and symbolized the fall of the ancien régime. Despite her controversial life, she remains a significant figure in French history, remembered for her tragic end and the turbulent times in which she lived.</p>\n"
              },
